@startuml

!include fta_metamodel.puml

' gtodo: Check with Jochen whether this AND gate and TransferInGate are correctly used here: Here it seems that the root cause is 
' essentially restating the failure mode (which is just a "contract violation") and in the end we will have a requirement which says
' that if the receiver is not called the correct number of times, an error should be returned. Do we really need to break this down 
' further e.g. with the AND gate or do we even need the FTA?
$FailureMode("Returns success although did not call receiver correct number of times", "Communication.ReturnsSuccessAlthoughDidNotCallReceiverCorrectNumberOfTimes")
$AndGate("AndGate1", "Communication.ReturnsSuccessAlthoughDidNotCallReceiverCorrectNumberOfTimes")
$IntermediateEvent("Did not call receiver correct number of times", "DidNotCallReceiverCorrectNumberOfTimes", "AndGate1")
$TransferInGate("CallbackNotCalledWithSamplesReceivedFromSkeleton", "DidNotCallReceiverCorrectNumberOfTimes")
$RootCause("Did not return an error", "DidNotReturnAnError", "AndGate1")

@enduml